# Build a Complete MERN Document Management Application

## 1. Role and Objective

Act as a senior full-stack software engineer, software architect, and UI/UX designer.

Build a complete, functional, maintainable, and placement-ready **Document Management System** using the MERN stack.

This application is intended to demonstrate my practical full-stack development skills during upcoming software engineering placement drives. The code should follow clean architecture, meaningful naming conventions, reliable error handling, and professional development practices.

**Important scope restriction:** Implement only the Document Management module. Do not implement AI chat, document question answering, RAG, embeddings, or an LLM integration. The core objective is to manage uploaded documents reliably.

Do not stop after generating a plan, architecture diagram, or sample code. Implement the complete application in the available project workspace, create all required files, connect the frontend to the actual backend, and verify the implementation.

If an existing project is present, inspect its files first, preserve useful existing functionality, and integrate the solution into its current structure rather than unnecessarily replacing the project.

